From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:22:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 103/148] [ae-patch] Keep the bulk-select bar inside a narrow
 sidebar

Reid reported on 2026-10-18 that the bulk-select bar overflows a narrow
sidebar: the exit button, "N selected" and the four action icons do not fit
in one pill at the sidebar's minimum width. The pill is now a container-query
container (2026-10-19). Below the width that fits the label, the bar shows the
bare count beside the icons; where there is room it shows "N selected" as
before. The label stays in the DOM as one text node, so screen readers always
hear "N selected", and the bare count is hidden from them. The threshold lives
in one AE file (AeBulkBarCount.tsx), to be tuned by screenshot at 220 px.
